 "puzzleThemes": [],
 "intro": {
  "text": "The Sicilian Defence, 1...c5, is the most popular answer to 1.e4. Black does not copy White in the centre. Instead the c-pawn fights for the d4 square, and when White opens the game with d4, Black trades that wing pawn for White's centre pawn. Black gets an extra centre pawn and an open road for the rooks on the c-file; White gets more space and quicker development. The games are sharp: White often plays in the centre or on the kingside, while Black fights back on the queenside."
 },
