      "text": "1...c5 controls d4 from the side instead of meeting e4 head on. If White plays d4, you can take with the c-pawn and swap a wing pawn for a centre pawn. 1...e5 is the other classical reply; 1...c5 leads to unbalanced positions where both sides have chances."
